IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra-definitions`
IMPORT `wra3-pt4-s77-84`

-- wra3-sch4.l4: the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, Schedule 4 (the housing credit element of state
-- pension credit). Part wra3, layer 1. Written from inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk
-- (version 2026-07-01), not the official text.
--
-- Host Acts (not among the sources): SPCA = State Pension Credit Act 2002; SSAA = Social Security Administration Act 1992.
-- The paragraph numbers of Schedule 4 are not printed in the text; they are counted from the Part headings and the
-- "is amended as follows" lines, and the count is corroborated by line 3033, which prints "(8)" for the paragraph that
-- repeals SPCA Sch 2 para 9(5)(a): Part 1 has paragraphs 1 to 8 (lines 3004, 3005, 3008, 3013, 3028, 3030, 3031, 3033) and
-- Part 2 paragraphs 9 to 14 (lines 3036, 3037, 3038, 3039, 3045, 3049). The numbers 9 to 14 are derived and uncorroborated.
-- Regulation-making powers (3A(5), 3A(6), SPCA 7(10)) and amendments that only add the words "housing credit" to a host list
-- are inert (reason 2). The conjunction helper is imported from the Part 4 module (the same three-valued "and").

§ `sch 4 Part 1 Amendments to the State Pension Credit Act 2002`

-- SPCA 3A(1): the first condition is that the claimant is liable to make payments in respect of the accommodation he
-- occupies as his home. What counts as "payments in respect of accommodation", liability, and occupying as a home is left
-- to regulations by 3A(5), so each limb is a MAYBE input (the regulations' answer, where supplied).
-- src:3015 | (1) The first of the conditions mentioned in section 1(2)(c)(iii) is that the claimant is liable to make payments in respect of the accommodation he occupies as his home.
@ref sch 4 para 4 SPCA 3A(1) (src:3015)
GIVEN `the claimant is liable to make payments in respect of the accommodation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claimant occupies the accommodation as his home` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 4 SPCA 3A(1) the first condition for housing credit is met` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first of the conditions ... is that the claimant is liable to make payments in respect of the accommodation he occupies as his home" (a limb fails)
    `s 78(6) the conjunction of the results` (LIST `the claimant is liable to make payments in respect of the accommodation`, `the claimant occupies the accommodation as his home`)

-- SPCA 3A(4): the accommodation must be in Great Britain and residential; it is immaterial whether it is the whole or
-- part of a building and whether or not it comprises separate and self-contained premises.
-- src:3018 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (1)—
-- src:3019 | (a) the accommodation must be in Great Britain;
-- src:3020 | (b) the accommodation must be residential accommodation;
-- src:3021 | (c) it is immaterial whether the accommodation consists of the whole or part of a building and whether or not it comprises separate and self-contained premises.
@ref sch 4 para 4 SPCA 3A(4) (src:3018-3021)
GIVEN `where the accommodation is` IS A Place
      `the accommodation is residential accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accommodation consists of the whole of a building` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accommodation comprises separate and self-contained premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 4 SPCA 3A(4) the accommodation is accommodation for the purposes of subsection (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) the accommodation must be in Great Britain": outside the United Kingdom or in Northern Ireland
        IF `where the accommodation is` EQUALS `outside the United Kingdom` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `where the accommodation is` EQUALS `Northern Ireland` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the accommodation must be residential accommodation"
        IF NOT `the accommodation is residential accommodation` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- (c) "it is immaterial whether the accommodation consists of the whole or part of a building and whether or not it comprises separate and self-contained premises": the last two inputs are never read
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- SPCA 3A(2): the second condition is that the claimant's capital and income are such that the amount of housing credit
-- payable (if entitled) would not be less than a prescribed amount.
-- src:3016 | (2) The second of the conditions mentioned in section 1(2)(c)(iii) is that the claimant's capital and income are such that the amount of the housing credit payable (if he were entitled to it) would not be less than a prescribed amount.
@ref sch 4 para 4 SPCA 3A(2) (src:3016)
GIVEN `the amount of the housing credit that would be payable if the claimant were entitled to it` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 3A(2)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 4 SPCA 3A(2) the second condition for housing credit is met` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amount regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 3A(2)`
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        IF `the amount of the housing credit that would be payable if the claimant were entitled to it` AT LEAST p
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second of the conditions ... is that ... the amount of the housing credit payable (if he were entitled to it) would not be less than a prescribed amount"
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the prescribed amount is left to regulations
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- SPCA 3A(3): where the claimant is entitled to a housing credit, the amount is an amount calculated in or determined
-- under regulations (which may be zero).
-- src:3017 | (3) Where the claimant is entitled to a housing credit, the amount of the housing credit shall be an amount calculated in or determined under regulations (which may be zero).
@ref sch 4 para 4 SPCA 3A(3) (src:3017)
GIVEN `the amount calculated in or determined under regulations` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 para 4 SPCA 3A(3) the amount of the housing credit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amount calculated in or determined under regulations`
    WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST n
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the amount is "calculated in or determined under regulations"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- Paragraph 2: SPCA 1(2)(c)(iii) names "the conditions in section 3A(1) and (2) (housing credit)" as a route to entitlement.
-- src:3005 | In section 1 (entitlement), in subsection (2)(c), at the end there is inserted
-- src:3006 | or
-- src:3007 | (iii) the conditions in section 3A(1) and (2) (housing credit).
@ref sch 4 para 2 SPCA 1(2)(c)(iii) (src:3005-3007)
GIVEN `the first condition in section 3A(1) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the second condition in section 3A(2) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 2 SPCA 1(2)(c)(iii) the claimant satisfies the conditions in section 3A(1) and (2)` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(iii) the conditions in section 3A(1) and (2) (housing credit)" a condition fails
    `s 78(6) the conjunction of the results` (LIST `the first condition in section 3A(1) is met`, `the second condition in section 3A(2) is met`)

-- Paragraph 3: SPCA 1(3)(c): entitlement to a housing credit, calculated in accordance with section 3A, if he satisfies the
-- conditions in subsections (1) and (2) of that section; and 1(3) as amended: entitlement to more than one of the credits
-- if he satisfies the relevant conditions.
-- src:3008 | In that section, in subsection (3)—
-- src:3009 | (a) after paragraph (b) there is inserted
-- src:3010 | or
-- src:3011 | (c) to a housing credit, calculated in accordance with section 3A, if he satisfies the conditions in subsections (1) and (2) of that section,
-- src:3012 | (b) for the words from “(or to both)” to the end there is substituted “ (or to more than one of them, if he satisfies the relevant conditions) ”.
@ref sch 4 para 3 SPCA 1(3) (src:3008-3012)
GIVEN `the claimant satisfies the conditions in subsections (1) and (2) of section 3A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 3 SPCA 1(3)(c) the claimant is entitled to a housing credit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the claimant satisfies the conditions in subsections (1) and (2) of section 3A`
    WHEN JUST TRUE  THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "entitled ... to a housing credit ... if he satisfies the conditions in subsections (1) and (2)" fails (a failed "if": a lawyer's reading (a))
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the conditions are satisfied has not been determined
    WHEN NOTHING    THEN NOTHING

@ref sch 4 para 3 SPCA 1(3)(b) (src:3012)
DECLARE `sch 4 para 3 credit` IS ONE OF
    `sch 4 para 3 guarantee credit`
    `sch 4 para 3 savings credit`
    `sch 4 para 3 housing credit`

@ref sch 4 para 3 SPCA 1(3)(b) (src:3012)
GIVEN `the claimant satisfies the relevant conditions for guarantee credit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant satisfies the relevant conditions for savings credit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant satisfies the relevant conditions for housing credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `sch 4 para 3 credit`
`sch 4 para 3 SPCA 1(3)(b) the credits the claimant is entitled to` MEANS
    -- "(or to more than one of them, if he satisfies the relevant conditions)": each credit whose relevant conditions are satisfied
    concat (LIST (IF `the claimant satisfies the relevant conditions for guarantee credit` THEN LIST `sch 4 para 3 guarantee credit` ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF `the claimant satisfies the relevant conditions for savings credit` THEN LIST `sch 4 para 3 savings credit` ELSE EMPTY),
                 (IF `the claimant satisfies the relevant conditions for housing credit` THEN LIST `sch 4 para 3 housing credit` ELSE EMPTY))

-- Paragraph 7: SPCA 17(1): "housing credit" shall be construed in accordance with sections 1 and 3A.
-- src:3031 | In section 17 (interpretation), in subsection (1), after the definition of “guarantee credit” there is inserted—
-- src:3032 | “housing credit” shall be construed in accordance with sections 1 and 3A;
@ref sch 4 para 7 SPCA 17(1) (src:3031-3032)
`sch 4 para 7 SPCA 17(1) housing credit is construed in accordance with` MEANS "sections 1 and 3A of the State Pension Credit Act 2002"

§ `sch 4 Part 2 Amendments to other Acts`

-- Paragraph 12: SSAA 122F(5): "housing credit" has the same meaning as in the State Pension Credit Act 2002.
-- src:3043 | (5) In this section “housing credit“ has the same meaning as in the State Pension Credit Act 2002
@ref sch 4 para 12 SSAA 122F(5) (src:3043)
`sch 4 para 12 SSAA 122F(5) housing credit has the same meaning as in` MEANS "the State Pension Credit Act 2002"
